qkm|a|Excelling; surpassing others in some good quality or the sum of qualities; of great worth; eminent, in a good sense; superior; as, an excellent man, artist, citizen, husband, discourse, book, song, etc.; excellent breeding, principles, aims, action. ; Superior in kind or degree, irrespective of moral quality; -- used with words of a bad significance.	j:8d8,49,4;w8u,46,6;2bo4,43,3;r09,34,2;1ct,33,6;296p,33,4;3fy,31,15;8qj,31,3;107k,30,9;1l4t,29,14;14p8,27,6;3fp,27,31;1rh3,27,6;4u8,25,3;1l55,24,3~3fp,27,31;1ovy,10,15;3fy,31,15;1l4t,29,14;1r8m,17,10;2a53,15,9;107k,30,9;qif,22,8;1rh3,27,6;14p8,27,6;w8u,46,6;1ct,33,6;27fd,19,5;296p,33,4;8d8,49,4	e:25v9,60,7;1fx8,34,5~25v9,60,7;1fx8,34,5
