r6k|a|Outward; exterior; relating to the outside, as of a body; being without; acting from without; -- opposed to internal; as, the external form or surface of a body. ; Outside of or separate from ourselves; (Metaph.) separate from the perceiving mind. ; Outwardly perceptible; visible; physical or corporeal, as distinguished from mental or moral. ; Not intrinsic nor essential; accidental; accompanying; superficial. ; Foreign; relating to or connected with foreign nations; as, external trade or commerce; the external relations of a state or kingdom. ; Away from the mesial plane of the body; lateral.	j:qia,94,6;1c2m,87,58;s5r,86,2;1ts9,79,2;1iw5,79,29;28h2,79,6;dip,74,8;1n7v,63,4;1rd4,59,13;1xwc,55,10;1iw4,53,5;udk,52,18;rg5,47,7;1m06,47,32;178m,46,7~1c2m,87,58;1m06,47,32;1iw5,79,29;1zf0,41,19;udk,52,18;xuk,31,13;1rd4,59,13;178f,38,12;1xwc,55,10;1uij,45,8;1xwa,34,8;dip,74,8;1wkn,41,8;1d8,33,8;21fw,27,7
